---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const title = 'About';
const description = `About ${SITE.name} — who writes it and how each post gets made.`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>

  <p>
    Hi, I'm {SITE.author}. I'm not a developer — I work a regular office job where, like a
    lot of people right now, I ended up relying on AI tools daily just to get through the
    work. That's the actual reason {SITE.name} exists: I kept hitting the same question —
    "is this new tool actually worth switching to, or is it just marketing" — and started
    writing down the answers for myself. This site is that, made public.
  </p>

  <p>
    Because of that background, I'm not writing as an engineer benchmarking model
    architectures. I'm writing as someone evaluating these tools the way most readers
    probably are: does it save real time, is it worth the subscription, what breaks when
    you actually try to use it for something that matters.
  </p>

  <h2>How posts get made</h2>
  <p>
    I'll be upfront about this rather than pretend otherwise: {SITE.name} runs on an
    AI-assisted publishing pipeline I built myself — research, drafting, and image
    generation are automated, but nothing goes live without me personally reviewing it
    first. I check claims, cut anything that doesn't hold up, and add real context from my
    own use where I have it. Where a claim is genuinely from hands-on testing, it reads
    that way; where it's drawn from public information or reporting instead, I try to keep
    the framing honest about that rather than implying first-hand experience I don't have.
    I'm not paid for positive coverage.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site is supported by display advertising (including Google AdSense) and may,
    in the future, include affiliate links clearly marked as such. Advertising and
    affiliate relationships never determine my conclusions.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections, or tips? Reach out on the <a href={withBase('/contact')}>contact page</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
